00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:15.530
It's eau de skin. Eau de skin.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.955
So, meet Natasha. Meet Jake.

00:00:16.955 --> 00:00:18.222
- Yes, great to meet you, man.

00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:20.850
- So, you are a world famous K-pop star,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.683
which everyone knows.

00:00:21.683 --> 00:00:22.516
- Not really.

00:00:22.516 --> 00:00:24.899
- Yes, you are, if you didn't know,

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:26.640
but I didn't know this about you.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.180
So, originally, you were like
an athlete from Hong Kong?

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.030
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.863
- Like, fencing?

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:31.872
- Yeah, I was a fencer.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:32.705
- Cool.

00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:33.747
- That's cool.

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:36.483
- My parents, they were Olympians too.

00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:37.316
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:37.316 --> 00:00:40.353
- My dad's a fencer, my mom's a gymnast.

00:00:40.353 --> 00:00:42.740
- Wow. So, I guess it
would have been a let down

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.490
if you didn't do something
in that category?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.488
- Yes, I mean, I was
prepping for London Olympics

00:00:48.488 --> 00:00:52.827
back then, and then while
prepping, I just told my parents,

00:00:52.827 --> 00:00:55.389
"Hey, you know what? I always
had this dream about music.

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:56.970
Let me do my thing."

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.992
- How did that go over?

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.664
- I mean, they want me of course

00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:04.410
to go to the Olympics,
y'know, do my thing.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.460
And it took me seven
months to persuade them.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.540
- Wow, but you were persistent.
That's a lot of months.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.410
- Yeah, they were really against me.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.270
And then they're like,
"You're out of your mind."

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:14.380
My principal told me that,

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.570
"This is the worst decision you're ever

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.051
gonna make in your life."

00:01:18.051 --> 00:01:19.384
- [Kelly] Have you sent him a letter?

00:01:19.384 --> 00:01:20.217
(audience laughter)

00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:22.270
- I think he knows by now he was wrong.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.143
- [Kelly] Or like a signed headshot.

00:01:24.143 --> 00:01:27.350
- Then, after I debuted as a singer,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.860
and I went back to have a
concert and I invited him

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.333
and he said, "Jackson,
we believed in you."

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.912
(laughter)

00:01:34.912 --> 00:01:36.537
We believed in you.

00:01:36.537 --> 00:01:39.620
- This happens! It happens!
That happened to me.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:43.777
I was like, "What!?"
People were totally like,

00:01:43.777 --> 00:01:45.970
"That's never gonna happen,
everybody has a dream,"

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.000
and then they were like, "the whole time."

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.387
You'd see them on the
news and they're like,

00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:50.830
"We believed from the beginning."

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:51.810
And I'm like, "You are a liar!"

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.240
- "We knew you were the one" Right? Right?

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:57.480
- So, were your parents
worried about you guys

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.320
in the entertainment
industry? Were they worried?

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.930
- Yeah! At first, I
said, "Hey! I passed this

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:05.810
audition in Korea. I'm
going, I'm leaving."

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.470
And then they're like, "Entertainment? No.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.200
They're gonna kidnap you
and put you in a cave-"

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.990
- Oh wow!
- [Kelly] What!?

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.180
- [Jackson] Y'know, like, parents.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.807
- Yeah.
- And then they were like,

00:02:15.807 --> 00:02:17.239
"No, you're not gonna do that.

00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:21.397
We're not gonna see you again.
You're gonna be MIA."

00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:24.885
And I'm like, "No, let me live my dream."

00:02:24.885 --> 00:02:29.600
And yes, seven months of
persuading and they're supportive.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.860
- That's amazing!

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.934
- Do we have to sit this far?
(laughter)

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:35.767
- You're just so cool
we're giving you room.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:36.783
(audience clapping)

00:02:36.783 --> 00:02:39.404
- [Natasha] We wanna adopt him!

00:02:39.404 --> 00:02:40.875
- [Kelly] We were giving you room.

00:02:40.875 --> 00:02:43.309
- Nobody's gonna kidnap ya, son.

00:02:43.309 --> 00:02:46.450
There's no caves for you,
you made it, kid!

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.634
You made it, kid!

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.420
- Unless it's really a
cool cave, with a bar.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.720
So, your new album is called
"Magic Man." Why that title?

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.890
Which is also a good song
by Heart, just saying.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.570
- The whole thing is
about a journey of finding

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.440
and exploring the new
me and deciding to drop

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.794
everything - whoever I
was, whatever I had before.

00:03:04.794 --> 00:03:09.584
To be as raw as possible that
I have ever been in my life.

00:03:09.584 --> 00:03:14.316
The album is called "Magic
Man," it's not just about music.

00:03:14.316 --> 00:03:17.550
The tone, the color, the
attitude, the visuals,

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.790
everything in one package and
that's who I am right now.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.130
- Are you into all of that?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.670
'Cause some artists aren't
into the whole thing,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.260
like into the art, into the
all of it, like the videos...

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.700
- No, I just wanna be me 'cause like

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.210
even though it fails, it could be bad,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.740
people can't relate to it,
but at least I won't regret it

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.740
'cause it's me, y'know?

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.097
- Someone said that to me
once the other day, like,

00:03:37.097 --> 00:03:38.337
"You're a sinking ship." And I was like,

00:03:38.337 --> 00:03:41.980
"Well, I'm still the captain,
so if it's gonna go down,

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.291
it's going to be because of me."

00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:46.364
And I'm not, by the way, I'm sorry!

00:03:46.364 --> 00:03:47.911
Write you a letter!

00:03:47.911 --> 00:03:52.617
It's one of those things where
I feel like in this industry,

00:03:52.617 --> 00:03:54.404
I can only speak for the music side of it,

00:03:54.404 --> 00:03:57.337
people do that. They
try and force you to be

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.270
whatever is popular or whatever,

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.650
and I kinda wanna do what
I'm feeling right now,

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.010
and it might be successful.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.630
I feel like every career does
this anyway, so it's fine.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.888
I love that you're knowing that so young.

00:04:07.888 --> 00:04:09.769
- I'm not young anymore.

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:12.573
- You're young comparatively speaking.

00:04:12.573 --> 00:04:15.210
So tell us about your new single.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.043
It's called "Blow," right?

00:04:16.043 --> 00:04:19.658
- Yes, that's the intro
of the whole album.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:24.130
It's another world that I'm
trying to bring all my audience

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.979
to - yeah, "Blow." This is "Blow."

00:04:26.979 --> 00:04:29.604
- [Kelly] I know, it's
amazing! This video is amazing.

00:04:29.604 --> 00:04:31.000
- [Jake] Beautiful, man.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.508
- [Jackson] If you have
time, please check it out.

00:04:33.508 --> 00:04:35.027
- [Jake] I have, yeah,
I listen to your music.

00:04:35.027 --> 00:04:36.840
- Well, if you have time,
please check it out.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.929
- I will do anything you
say. I wanna adopt you.

00:04:39.929 --> 00:04:41.954
- [Kelly] And take you to her cave.

00:04:41.954 --> 00:04:43.853
- He's so vulnerable and cute!

00:04:43.853 --> 00:04:46.789
- This is how it starts, and
then you end up in a cave.

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:49.062
- We are those who kidnapped-

00:04:49.062 --> 00:04:51.927
- Oh, that was what my
